# Example EnvironmentFile for contrib/systemd/pyck-debug-worker-update.service.
#
# Only needed while the GitHub repo is private; public releases download
# anonymously. Install at this path, mode 0600, owned by root:
#
#   sudo install -m 0600 pyck-debug-worker-update.sysconfig.example \
#     /etc/sysconfig/pyck-debug-worker-update
#
# Deliberately a separate file from /etc/sysconfig/pyck-debug-worker, so the
# token never ends up in the worker's environment.
#
# Create the token on GitHub: Settings → Developer settings → Fine-grained
# personal access token → Resource owner: pyck-ai → Only select repositories:
# pyck-ai/pyck-debug-worker → Repository permissions: Contents: Read-only.
#
# GitHub deploy keys do NOT work: they are SSH/git-only and cannot download
# release assets.

#GITHUB_TOKEN=
